  Counts: True 13, False 6, Unknown 7, Fiction 2. Four
  closed, four discovered — the frontier moved, it did
  not shrink.ROUND 4 — The retest; the bracket re-anchors (EE 369)

The seat-balanced retest of the founding claim (U6) completed:
starter 16, v1 10, random 14 over 40 episodes. Read together
with T6, the lineage's first-evening narrative inverts: the
"always take lethal" change was celebrated on a confounded
receipt, and the tracker now holds the correction at the same
prominence as the claim. This is the MOAT/TLUF discipline
doing its work — a False-adjacent finding kept visible, the
registry more accurate than the story.

Standing after Round 4:
  - Champion title: SUSPENDED in fact (the charter keeps v1
    listed until evidence names a successor; the registry no
    longer asserts v1 exceeds the starter).
  - v3b and v3c remain co-candidates (U3, U4): both beat v1 in
    both seat legs. Their anchor tests against the STARTER —
    the honest baseline — are running: v3b xreq_726f3ec8 +
    xreq_fedb848e; v3c xreq_1cd68615 + xreq_9a3fe5ae.
  - The veteran seat remains the strongest single bloc per
    appearance across every test tonight (roughly a third of
    all episodes). The gap to the field is the real target;
    heuristic micro-tuning around the starter is not.ROUND 5 — Anchor tests against the starter (EE 369-370)

The co-candidates were re-anchored on the honest baseline, the
pristine starter, seat-balanced, 40 episodes each:

  v3b vs starter (xreq_726f3ec8 + xreq_fedb848e, $0.108):
    starter 17, v3b 9, random 14. REFUTED as an advance (F3).
  v3c vs starter (xreq_1cd68615 + xreq_9a3fe5ae, $0.141):
    v3c 16, starter 12, random 12. OPEN (U7) — nominally
    ahead, legs split by seat.

Standing at EE 370, stated plainly: after ~300 hosted episodes
and five variants, no variant has a verified claim to beating
the bundled starter bot. v3c is the only live candidate. The
veteran field (random seat) took roughly a third of every
test's episodes throughout — the gap to the field is in deck
construction and multi-way threat judgement, not in the swing
scoring this bracket has been tuning. Next honest moves, in
